    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Delivery semantics: the defect, the fix, and what the store forgot",
      "description": "Kafka gives AT-LEAST-ONCE, so a record can arrive twice. These four lines are the whole story of what that costs and whether the idempotency store is covering it.\n\nDOUBLE APPLIED is the defect: a record whose effect ran for a key the effect had already run for. On the at-least-once arm (KL_DEDUPE=false) it climbs whenever a fault is injected. On the dedupe arm it should stay flat at zero.\n\nSUPPRESSED is the fix doing its job: a redelivery the store recognised, whose effect did not run. It is zero unless dedupe is on, and the two arms trade places on these first two lines.\n\nEVICTIONS and EXPIRIES are the honesty lines, and they are why the other two can be believed. The store is BOUNDED: it drops keys to stay under capacity and drops them for age. A dropped key reads as first-seen when its redelivery arrives, the effect runs again, and nothing looks wrong. So a non-zero double-apply count on the dedupe arm means one of two opposite things \u2014 a broken store, or a store that was simply too small \u2014 and only these lines tell you which. A measured duplicate figure taken from a run where either is non-zero is measuring the store, not the delivery semantics.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "kafka-lab-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "axisLabel": "records"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      },
